  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: High temperatures throughout Northern\nand Central Nevada this afternoon will be six to eight degrees\nbelow normal for this time of year. A ridge of high pressure \nwill build eastward across Northern Nevada Sunday into Monday. As\na result, a warming trend is expected Sunday and Monday. By Monday\nafternoon, maximum temperatures across Northern and Central Nevada\nwill be near normal for this time of year. \n\nA trough of low pressure will move eastward across Northern \nNevada Monday afternoon through Tuesday morning, resulting in a\nslight chance of valley rain and mountain snow. Any precipitation\nassociated with this atmospheric disturbance will remain north \nof Interstate 80. Precipitation chances will be highest near the\nNevada/Idaho border. Zonal flow aloft is anticipated Wednesday and\nThursday. This will result in dry weather and seasonal \ntemperatures. The next storm system may begin to impact Northern \nand Central Nevada as early as Thursday night. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding unseasonably cool conditions this afternoon. High\nforecast confidence in a warming trend Sunday and Monday. Low \nforecast confidence in the possibility of valley rain and mountain\nsnow in Northern Nevada Monday afternoon through Tuesday morning.\nNo deviations from the NBM model output.",
